---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const updated = 'July 31, 2026';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions — Therapy Appointment Reminder Service | The Engine Room Financial Group"
  description="Terms and conditions for the text message therapy appointment reminder service operated by The Engine Room Financial Group on behalf of the healthcare facilities it serves. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to cancel, HELP for help."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Terms & Conditions"
  intro="Therapy Appointment Reminder Service — the text message program operated by The Engine Room Financial Group on behalf of the healthcare facilities we serve. Enrollment is voluntary and free to enroll."
  updated={updated}
>
  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">01</span>Program Summary</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>Program name</dt>
      <dd>Therapy Appointment Reminder Service</dd>
      <dt>Operated by</dt>
      <dd>
        The Engine Room Financial Group, on behalf of the healthcare facility
        named in each message
      </dd>
      <dt>Who receives it</dt>
      <dd>
        Outpatient therapy patients of a participating facility who have given
        written consent
      </dd>
      <dt>Message content</dt>
      <dd>
        Appointment reminders, reschedule notices, cancellation notices, and
        confirmation replies
      </dd>
      <dt>Frequency</dt>
      <dd>
        Varies by your appointment schedule — typically one reminder per
        scheduled appointment
      </dd>
      <dt>Cost</dt>
      <dd>Free to enroll. Message and data rates may apply.</dd>
      <dt>To cancel</dt>
      <dd>Reply STOP to any message</dd>
      <dt>For help</dt>
      <dd>
        Reply HELP, or call your facility. Perkins Country Manor outpatient
        therapy: <a href="tel:6067562156">(606) 756-2156</a>
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">02</span>What This Program Is</h2>
    <p>
      The Therapy Appointment Reminder Service sends text message reminders about
      scheduled outpatient therapy appointments. Messages are sent by The Engine
      Room Financial Group (&ldquo;ERFG&rdquo;) on behalf of the healthcare
      facility that scheduled your appointment, under a written services
      agreement with that facility.
    </p>
    <p>
      The first participating facility is Perkins Country Manor, operated by
      Bracken KY Opco LLC, in Augusta, Kentucky. Additional facilities may
      participate over time; the facility responsible for your care is always
      identified by name in the message you receive.
    </p>
    <p>Messages you may receive include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A reminder of the date and time of an upcoming therapy appointment, which
        may ask you to reply YES to confirm or NO to cancel
      </li>
      <li>A notice that an appointment has been rescheduled</li>
      <li>A notice that an appointment has been cancelled</li>
      <li>
        A reply to a STOP or HELP request, or a confirmation of your enrollment
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">03</span>This Is Not Marketing</h2>
    <div class="legal-callout">
      <p>
        This program sends transactional appointment communications only. It does
        not send marketing, promotional, or advertising content, and it does not
        deliver messages on behalf of any third-party advertiser. The Engine Room
        Financial Group acts solely as a contracted service provider and HIPAA
        business associate of the healthcare facility named in each message.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p>
      Your mobile phone number and your consent are never shared, sold, rented,
      or transferred to third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional
      purposes. See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for full detail.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">04</span>Enrollment Is Voluntary</h2>
    <div class="legal-callout">
      <p>
        Enrollment is entirely voluntary. Consent to receive text messages is not
        a condition of receiving therapy services, scheduling an appointment,
        being admitted, or completing any purchase or transaction. Declining to
        enroll, or opting out later, will not affect your care in any way.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p>
      You enroll by signing a standalone written consent form presented to you at
      your facility, separate from admission and treatment paperwork. On that
      form you provide your own mobile number and indicate affirmatively that you
      wish to receive messages. Facility staff do not enroll patients on their
      behalf.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">05</span>Message Frequency</h2>
    <p>
      Message frequency varies based on your appointment schedule. In typical
      use, you will receive one reminder message per scheduled appointment, plus
      an additional message if that appointment is rescheduled or cancelled. You
      will not receive recurring messages unrelated to a scheduled appointment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">06</span>Cost</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Message and data rates may apply.</strong> The program is provided
      to you at no charge, but your wireless carrier may charge you for sending
      or receiving text messages according to your plan. Contact your carrier for
      details about your messaging plan.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">07</span>How to Stop Messages</h2>
    <p>
      You may stop receiving messages at any time by replying <strong>STOP</strong
      > to any message from the program. You will receive a single confirmation
      message, and then no further messages will be sent.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may also ask any staff member at your facility to remove you, or
      contact us using the details below. Removal takes effect within one
      business day.
    </p>
    <p>
      Opting out affects text messages only. Your facility may still contact you
      about your appointments by phone or by mail.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">08</span>How to Get Help</h2>
    <p>
      Reply <strong>HELP</strong> to any message to receive program information
      and support contact details.
    </p>
    <p>
      For questions about your appointment or your care, contact your facility
      directly. For Perkins Country Manor outpatient therapy, call
      <a href="tel:6067562156">(606) 756-2156</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      For questions about the messaging program itself, contact ERFG at
      <a href="mailto:getintouch@TheERFG.com">getintouch@TheERFG.com</a> or
      <a href="tel:5168780015">(516) 878-0015</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">09</span>Delivery and Carrier Liability</h2>
    <p>
      Text message delivery depends on your wireless carrier and on conditions
      outside our control. <strong
        >Wireless carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered
        messages.</strong
      > We cannot guarantee that any individual message will be delivered or
      delivered on time.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because of this, appointment reminders are a convenience and not a
      substitute for your own record of your appointments. Please do not rely
      solely on a text message to know when your appointment is scheduled.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">10</span>Supported Carriers</h2>
    <p>
      The program is available on major United States wireless carriers. Carrier
      participation and support may change without notice, and carriers are not
      responsible for the content of program messages.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">11</span>Keeping Your Number Current</h2>
    <p>
      Please tell your facility if your mobile number changes or is
      reassigned, so reminders are not sent to someone else. If you receive
      reminders that are not intended for you, reply STOP or call the facility
      number above and we will remove the number.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">12</span>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Information collected through this program is handled as described in our
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. Appointment information relating to
      your treatment is protected health information under HIPAA, and ERFG
      operates as a business associate of your facility with respect to it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="legal-num">13</span>Changes to These Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. The effective date above reflects the current
      version, and the current version is always posted at this address.
      Continuing to participate in the program after an update constitutes
      acceptance of the updated terms; you may opt out at any time by replying
      STOP.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
